- op: discuss  # 601c
  at: '2026-05-21T09:40:11Z'  # 601c
  by: agent  # 601c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 601c
  clock: 8  # 601c
  nonce: 601c  # 601c
  message: "Closed in PR #3862 (commit 41484d271c). Two heuristics added in cmd_dead_code_maybe: (1) usage_contexts view_func cross-reference — symbols at position=view_func in usage_contexts join the BFS seed set (only callable-position entries seed; arg_value etc. are ignored); (2) polymorphic dispatch demotion — for each dead method, walk transitive ancestors via extends/inherits/implements edges; if any ancestor's same-named method is reachable, demote. Summary surfaces demoted_view_func and demoted_dispatch_inherited counts. Empirical on hypergumbo self-analysis: demoted_view_func=8; demoted_dispatch_inherited=0 (hypergumbo's DefUseExtractor/NameMatcher families use Python Protocol/duck typing, not classical inheritance, so the strict heuristic correctly finds no overrides). Classical-inheritance codebases should see substantially more demotions. Heuristics #2 (framework lifecycle convention list) and #4 (confidence annotation) from the WI-vuton plan are deferred — they need non-trivial pattern enumeration and a schema change. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: the FP-reduction impact depends on the inheritance-edge density of the target codebase."  # 601c
